## Why This Is Asked

Designing a multi-tenant scheduler that preserves per-tenant ordering while adapting quotas to burstiness tests deep knowledge of backpressure, fairness, and liveness. It also challenges how to measure and guarantee fairness across tenants in a shared resource.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant FIFO queues
- Global bounded backlog with backpressure signaling
- Dynamic quotas via token buckets adjusted by observed burstiness
- Scheduling policy (weighted RR) to prevent starvation
- Observability: per-tenant throughput, latency, and starvation windows

